{"id":"8c6c7289-417e-4331-803f-83efced2df02","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b41279e3b46e27a4","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/playground.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"7a38d0897d5dcb8828522d30401e845b2bb36578","start":31,"end":95},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","SharedWorkspace","}","from","\"","../shared/playground-link","\""]},"context":{"after":"779b9e943e48c349"}},"payload":{"text":"TypeScript Playground links (shared/playground-link.ts), both ways. Swap the host of a playground link for the editor's\nand it opens here as a real workspace: an editor of its own (an instance, shared/instance.ts, named by the link), so\nfollowing a link never replaces the workspace you're in, and reloading it keeps what you've changed since. And the top\nbar's Share writes your workspace as a Playground v2 link, which opens here or in the TypeScript Playground.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:45:46.248Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:45:46.248Z"}
